  "content": {
    "id": "p13-q15-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "15",
    "prompt": "There are 10 votes cast in an election for candidate $A$ and candidate $B$. The final tally is 6 to 4, respectively.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p13-q15-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "How many ways can this happen?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "210.",
          "worked": "Arrange six identical $A$ votes and four identical $B$ votes:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=\\frac{10!}{6!4!}\\\\N&=210.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q15-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "How many ways can this happen if it is known that candidate $A$ stayed ahead of $B$ while counting the votes?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "42.\n\nThe first vote must be for $A$; subtract the remaining sequences that allow $B$ to overtake the remaining $A$ count.",
          "worked": "The first vote must be $A$. The remaining five $A$ votes and four $B$ votes must have at least as many $A$ votes as $B$ votes in every prefix, so that the original count stays strictly ahead.\n\nThere are $\\dfrac{9!}{5!4!}$ unrestricted remaining sequences. For an invalid sequence, interchange $A$ and $B$ through the first prefix in which $B$ exceeds $A$. This gives a sequence with six $A$ votes and three $B$ votes. Conversely, interchange through the first prefix in which $A$ exceeds $B$ to recover the invalid sequence. Hence the invalid sequences number $\\dfrac{9!}{6!3!}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=\\frac{9!}{5!4!}-\\frac{9!}{6!3!}\\\\N&=126-84\\\\N&=42.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 80
      }
    ]
  },
